00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:30.680
The World Health Organization included "Gaming Disorder" as the latest version in its Disease Classification Manual.

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:34.460
We've talked about this before, but now it's finally been made official.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:41.740
World Heath Organization, W.H.O, has announced "gaming disorder" is a thing. It's a real thing.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:46.580
Now I'm kind of on the fence on this. I don't really know where I stand to be honest.

00:12:46.760 --> 00:12:48.760
I really do see both sides.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:13:00.240
A lot of people are questioning this move, scientists specifically, saying "there was lack of good quality scientific evidence about how to properly diagnose video game addiction."

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:05.540
Also arguing the point that "we're essentially pathologizing a hobby."

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:10.880
"What's next? Tanning addiction, dance addiction, exercise addiction..."

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:13.000
But no one is having a conversation about them.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:19.160
And I kind of- I really do understand this point. Why is gaming specifically being targeted here?

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:27.860
It seems like it's just a very popular topic right now. But, why is gaming getting- taking the whole beating?Essentially,

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:31.380
it's an addiction, yeah, but why is "gaming disorder" a thing?

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:40.760
I was heavily addicted, I have no doubt about that, I just- I denied it for many, many years. You know, saying that "oh yeah, I really need it when I travel away, it's so important."

00:13:40.940 --> 00:13:44.360
Whereas I wasn't sort of really confronting the issue itself.

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:47.540
(laughs) So... (laughs) what?

00:13:47.680 --> 00:13:51.740
The World Champion winner of Snooker says he was addicted.

00:13:51.740 --> 00:13:53.660
That's how he got World Champion...

00:13:53.940 --> 00:14:01.520
You could say that anyone that tries to get an Olympic medal- "Oh you're just.. uh you're just addicted...to training." "You're training every single day!"

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:02.480
(laughs)

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:05.420
"You don't even let them have games at all?"

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:09.940
"I have so far managed to resist-"
"How old are they?" "They are 6 and 8."

00:14:09.940 --> 00:14:18.620
But I- I really do question the, uh, how sensible it is to invite something that we know is very addictive. Computer games are very addictive.

00:14:18.720 --> 00:14:26.700
So with Fortnite getting so popular, especially with young kids, a lot of parents are discussing this right now as well. It's obviously a very

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:28.080
popular topic.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:32.640
This women saying that she doesn't even let her kids play video games at all,

00:14:32.760 --> 00:14:35.000
